    "notes": "Inspected 70 current frames: 13 portable, 13 shared-material/geographic, 25 medium-fi and 19 native. The complete mapped crossing has two concrete box-girder decks, three haunched river spans, regular approach spans, paired supports, six traffic lanes, outside paths, open metal barriers and repeating double-arm lights. Near levels retain chamfered pier heads, caps, bearings, joints, rail posts and lamp housings. The street level simplifies columns and fittings while retaining the defining crossing shape. Widened only the small landing caps after the native review found a mapped path edge just outside the old footprint."
  },
